<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  LaunchDaemon for the UPDATE HALF — `roomlerd update-helper`.

  Why this exists: `installer -pkg … -target /` requires root, and the
  DEFAULT macOS install is the per-user LaunchAgent alone (the privileged
  overlay daemon is opt-in). So a default install could never self-update:
  the agent either failed the install silently (pre-rc.469 it then exited 0
  and `KeepAlive{SuccessfulExit=false}` left the machine OFFLINE — field
  2026-08-25) or, after that fix, refused forever. This unit is the missing
  root half of updating, and nothing else: no enrollment, no control WS, no
  agent row — it resolves the PUBLIC release feed, verifies, installs, and
  exits. The agents merely signal it.

  It also removes the whole exit-to-update failure class on two-half Macs:
  no agent process is ever the installer's parent and none exits for an
  update — the pkg's postinstall re-bootstraps both halves, and the helper
  is not long-running, so there is nothing to race.

  Wake sources, all three deliberate:
    RunAtLoad      — catch up right after boot / first install.
    StartInterval  — the periodic cadence (owned HERE, not by the agents;
                     one owner of "check+download+verify+install").
    WatchPaths     — the trigger file the agents touch on rc:agent.update.
                     /var/tmp is sticky/world-writable ON PURPOSE: the
                     per-user agent is not root, and the trigger is
                     ADVISORY-ONLY — whoever writes it can cause an update
                     CHECK, never choose what gets installed (the helper
                     independently resolves and verifies the release, and
                     the install-storm cooldown bounds spam).

  Not KeepAlive: the helper runs, decides, exits. launchd relaunches it on
  the next wake source. ThrottleInterval guards a crash-looping helper.

  ⚠️ postinstall must NEVER bootout a LOADED com.roomler.update — during an
  update the postinstall is a grandchild of this very job, and booting the
  job kills the whole process group, `installer` included, mid-payload. It
  bootstraps only when not yet loaded; a CHANGED plist therefore takes
  effect at next boot, which is acceptable for a file that rarely changes.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.roomler.update</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Library/Roomler/roomlerd.app/Contents/MacOS/roomlerd</string>
        <string>update-helper</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- 6 h — mirrors the agents' old 4 h ± the reality that pushes cover
         the urgent case; the interval is the wedge-heal ceiling only. -->
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>21600</integer>

    <key>WatchPaths</key>
    <array>
        <string>/private/var/tmp/meshharbor-update-check</string>
    </array>

    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>60</integer>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/var/log/roomler/update.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/var/log/roomler/update.log</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>RUST_LOG</key>
        <string>info</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
